  "family": {
    "title": "Family",
    "summary": "Family words come in pairs: plain 兄 and 姉 when you talk about your own family to others, polite お兄さん and お姉さん for someone else's — or when you speak to your own. 兄弟 is written with brothers but covers sisters too: it is the everyday word for siblings.",
